      <div type="work" n="95">
        <pb n="135"/>
        <head>95 — iv — VII. — <quote>Let the heavens rejoice and let the earth be glad</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="1">A great wonder! they<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> who once were darkness have become light : upon<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> them who were deprived of mercy mercy has now come. They who were destitute of God are now made a dwelling-place of the Spirit : with whom let us praise God the only good and merciful one.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 135, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. xcvi, 11.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 135, n. 3</orig></choice> Hos. ii, 23-25.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 135, n. 4</orig></choice> Rom. ix, 22-26 <quote>But, if..... and her that had not been loved beloved. For it shall be..... sons of the living God.</quote></note>
      </noteGrp>
    </body>
